{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0186oxVVnLNVxTQuSbFuXv7E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tstatic struct sk_buff *fou_gro_receive(struct sock *sk,\n2\t\t\t\t\t       struct list_head *head,\n3\t\t\t\t\t       struct sk_buff *skb)\n4\t{\n5\t\tconst struct net_offload __rcu **offloads;\n6\t\tstruct fou *fou = fou_from_sock(sk);\n7\t\tconst struct net_offload *ops;\n8\t\tstruct sk_buff *pp = NULL;\n9\t\tu8 proto;\n10\t\n11\t\tif (!fou)\n12\t\t\tgoto out;\n13\t\n14\t\tproto = fou->protocol;\n15\t\n16\t\t/* We can clear the encap_mark for FOU as we are essentially doing\n17\t\t * one of two possible things.  We are either adding an L4 tunnel\n18\t\t * header to the outer L3 tunnel header, or we are simply\n19\t\t * treating the GRE tunnel header as though it is a UDP protocol\n20\t\t * specific header such as VXLAN or GENEVE.\n21\t\t */\n22\t\tNAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->encap_mark = 0;\n23\t\n24\t\t/* Flag this frame as already having an outer encap header */\n25\t\tNAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->is_fou = 1;\n26\t\n27\t\toffloads = NAPI_GRO_CB(skb)->is_ipv6 ? inet6_offloads : inet_offloads;\n28\t\tops = rcu_dereference(offloads[proto]);\n29\t\tif (!ops || !ops->callbacks.gro_receive)\n30\t\t\tgoto out;\n31\t\n32\t\tpp = call_gro_receive(ops->callbacks.gro_receive, head, skb);\n33\t\n34\tout:\n35\t\treturn pp;\n36\t}\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8d442dc-684e-4461-bf53-b09ba88deb81","uuid":"a73bfc34-0b93-4df8-939f-00a681040f2d","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:34:01.794Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/yangkaiyan/Desktop/EECS4080/blind-run/samples/s179.c","content":"static struct sk_buff *fou_gro_receive(struct sock *sk,\n\t\t\t\t       struct list_head *head,\n\t\t\t\t       struct sk_buff *skb)\n{\n\tconst struct net_offload __rcu **offloads;\n\tstruct fou *fou = fou_from_sock(sk);\n\tconst struct net_offload *ops;\n\tstruct sk_buff *pp = NULL;\n\tu8 proto;\n\n\tif (!fou)\n\t\tgoto out;\n\n\tproto = fou->p